plugin-qualify (0.18.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * version 0.18.2: the notes name the isolated step (#249)
  * The sweep test allows for the hanger's isolated step, and checks its
    record shows it (#249)
  * version 0.18.2: a silent instrument under the adapter, and a pin for a
    percent-encoded name
  * isolated_signal opens libjack at run time, as jack_peak does, and the
    package needs no JACK to build or install (#249)
  * isolated step: each command has the sync's budget, so a plugin that hangs
    in add ends there (#249)
  * isolated step: a probe's crash or hang stays its outcome, the tool is
    executable, the package check names isolated_signal (#249)
  * The descriptor round trip counts the spaced fixture
  * The adapter run's level problem is not an unmeasured-reason word
  * qualify-rejudge test: the step owed on the record that reads isolated
    (#249)
  * Old isolated records stay offered and owe the step; a new record missing
    a step is refused (#249)
  * README: the isolated step and --isolated-only (#249)
  * The isolated step: an RT-unsafe plugin is isolated only once it ran
    alone, in the same pass (#249)
  * clap-qualify, lv2_measure: each cost figure prints the policy it was
    timed under (#214)
  * An LV2 file named by a percent-encoded IRI gets a pin
  * A silent instrument under a held note does not read as qualified

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:07:50 +0000
